{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/319728-abuse-survivors","id":319728,"title":"Abuse survivors","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-23T01:42:40-08:00","id":319728,"title":"Abuse survivors","content":"Changelings are survivors of abuse, yes? Their seemings are scars; their courts are ways of dealing with that little fact (hedonistic escapism, violent acting-out and revenge fantasies, abused-turns-abuser, paranoia). <br /> <br /> One thing I'm particularly curious about is how other people portray this particular aspect of the Changeling way of being in their games. Nightmares of Faerie and one's Keeper?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T02:50:49-08:00","id":319766,"title":"","content":"Autumn are not abused-turn-abusers - or at least aren't anymore than any of the other Courts - that phenomenon occurs in all of them.<br /> <br /> The Courts represent the archetypical stages of dealing with grief/recovery.<br /> <br /> Spring: Denial<br /> Summer: Anger<br /> Autumn: Bargaining<br /> Winter: Depression","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T03:08:44-08:00","id":319776,"title":"","content":"Changelings<i> can be </i>abuse survivors. It is an excellent metaphor, and not completely a metaphor. However, they don't have to be, especially if the player is uncomfortable with that. A CHangeling could have simply run away because they miss home, or a Keeper could have become bored with them and sent them away.<br /> <br /> It depends on the group how much you want to play up &quot;Seemings as scars&quot; vs. &quot;new Faerie Forms&quot;. You can play Changeling with a number of different comfort levels with the metaphor. None of this is in any way disagreeing with the OP, of course, just noting variations in style. It's interesting how in the rulebook the beginning ran heavy with Changelings-as-victems then moved into magical wonder as it went on. Not a criticism, indeed...it's anouther good metaphor.<br /> <br /> My current game has both Changelings who were clearly abused (like Calamity), Changelings who were more or less complicit with their Keeper (like Insincere Marguerite) and Changelings who were too wrapped up in their role to notice till they broke free (like Gawain or Ace) or some combination thereof (like Jacob or Lorelei). One thing they are discovering is how...different people memories...and opinions...of Faerie are. To hear one PC mourning the loss of the innocent girl she once was and hating her Keeper for it, while anouther loathed her racist past before being taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T08:10:42-08:00","id":319893,"title":"","content":"David Hill clarified that the idea is that they are survivors rather than explicitly abuse survivors. Going to other media for an example, look at the recent Tomb Raider or the book Hatchet. Rather obvious, but still very applicable.<br /> <br /> The idea is rather that the Fae and their Domains manifest moments of radical life change. A child who can't fault either parent for splitting can still find a Durance in the separation, as metaphorically it was (for the child at least) a moment of inevitability that swept in and completely changed their life-rather like the Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T08:48:37-08:00","id":319911,"title":"","content":"There is of course nothing wrong with playing Changelings as abuse survivors, but as said before, there is more to it than that. The Changeling I run now was not badly treated in Arcadia, but had her own reasons to escape and defy her Keeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T19:04:18-08:00","id":320306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/319728-abuse-survivors?p=319766#post319766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Autumn are not abused-turn-abusers - or at least aren't anymore than any of the other Courts - that phenomenon occurs in all of them.<br /> <br /> The Courts represent the archetypical stages of dealing with grief/recovery.<br /> <br /> Spring: Denial<br /> Summer: Anger<br /> Autumn: Bargaining<br /> Winter: Depression</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always &quot;liked&quot; how Acceptance was missing from that list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T05:38:21-0